# DTF tier manifest: scanner-adapter-java-db
#   (artifact-keeper#5913, scanner adapter 1.7.1)
# Profile-set: filesystem + trivy (the scanner-adapter sidecar,
# SCANNER_ADAPTER_IMAGE; the red/green axis is the adapter image). The oracle
# recreates the adapter with fixtures/java-db-unreachable.yml on top, then
# without it. Images are built at run time (fixtures/mkimage.py: alpine-shaped,
# libcrypto1.1 1.1.1c-r0, so Trivy reports CVEs; `jar` adds
# /opt/app/lib/log4j-core-2.14.1.jar, which makes trivy open its Java DB) and
# pushed through /v2.
# NETWORK: the adapter downloads the Trivy DB from ghcr.io (~100 MiB,
# pre-warmed in setup) and the trivy Java DB from mirror.gcr.io
# (trivy-java-db:1, ~1 GiB compressed, ~1.5 GiB unpacked) once. Disk: pre-fix,
# every concurrent first JAR scan stages its own copy (~1.9 GiB each).
#
# WHAT IS GATED
#   #5913 trivy downloads its Java DB into the adapter's cache on demand, in
#         every trivy process that meets a JAR. Concurrent first JAR scans
#         unpacked over each other and failed ("chmod
#         .../java-db/trivy-java.db: no such file or directory"). The adapter
#         now downloads it once (single flight, file lock across replicas),
#         every scan runs with --skip-java-db-update, and a scan that needs
#         it before it is there waits for that download and runs again. When
#         the Java DB cannot be fetched, images without JARs still scan.
#
# THE CASES
#   (CONTROL) Java DB unreachable, SCANNER_TRIVY_SKIP_DB_UPDATE=true, empty
#     Java DB cache: an image with no JAR scans to completion with its CVEs
#     (a fix that fails every scan when the Java DB download fails, like the
#     first attempt in PR 6055, breaks this).
#   (CONTROL) same adapter: an image with a JAR fails closed (never completed
#     with 0 findings), naming the Java DB.
#   (FIX #5913) adapter recreated with the Java DB reachable and its cache
#     still empty; three JAR images scanned at once: all three complete with
#     findings, and the adapter logged one Java DB download. Pre-fix: the
#     concurrent trivy downloads race and scans fail.
#   (CONTROL) a JAR image scanned after that completes (the Java DB is reused).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: registry pushes and scan polls back to back.
COVERS="5913"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem scanners.trivy"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
